A||||9||Kwez||how to ID an 88||||1||
Z||000000||Kwez||05-31-2001||02:19 PM||||what's a sure fire way to know if a Fiero is a (real) 88 ?<BR>can it be checked from the VIN ?<P>thx||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||05-31-2001||02:24 PM||||88 is a J in position 10 of the vin.<P>You'd see HPxxxxxx for 87<BR>and JPxxxxxx for 88 for the last 8 VIN characters.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-31-2001||02:25 PM||||here is the rest of the VIN info too:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.nytmare.org/fiero/vin/fierovin.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nytmare.org/fiero/vin/fierovin.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||05-31-2001||03:20 PM||||Or look under the rear suspension. No mistake there unless you are not familiar with the pre-88s.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jay||05-31-2001||04:58 PM||||Usually you can tell from the rims.  Rears have a lip, fronts don't.  Or is it the other way around?  Not always accurate as some have  put 88 rims on pre-88 cars.  <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kick.gif">  <BR>THE NORTHSTAR GIVES YOU A REAL KICK IN THE ASS!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||LZeitgeist||05-31-2001||05:44 PM||||On the '88's, the front GT/Formula wheels have no lip; the matching rears have a 1" wide lip. <P>Conversely, if the car in question has "lipped" rims all the way around, or if it has the 14" Hi Tech rims, the front wheels will stick out just a bit farther than pure aesthetics would like. (Even on the '88's, the 14" Hi Tech rims were the same all the way around - they had the same lip on the front as on the rear of the car).||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||05-31-2001||05:52 PM||||88s have vented rotors and aluminum suspension pieces under the rear. <BR>Pre-88s have solid rotors and stamped steel rear control arms. <BR>Pre-88 rear toe links are toward the back of the cradle. 88 rear toe links are toward the front of the cradle.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||05-31-2001||06:10 PM||||Also 88's have the dot matrix dash panels. VIN is the sure fire way.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierochic88||05-31-2001||06:13 PM||||Also if an 88 GT has the original paint the car is entirely monochromatic and only available in the following colors:<P>Red   Yellow  Silver  White  <BR>Medium Red Metallic  and Black<P>no Blue's or Gold's<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Kwez||05-31-2001||09:28 PM||||wow, lotsa answers on this one !<BR>I'll always try to check for ALL the clues, better safe than sorry.<P>thanks guys (& gals ;-)||||reg||1
